  "considered": [
    "Pixabay, MarjanNo, \"Flowers, Drawing, Child's Drawing\" (https://pixabay.com/photos/flowers-tulips-children-drawing-3311082/), Pixabay Content License. Real oil pastel tulips with stems. Set aside: a heavier, flatter pastel hand than the crayon set.",
    "Pixabay, EME, \"To Paint Children Drawing Sun\" (https://pixabay.com/photos/to-paint-children-drawing-sun-day-537195/), Pixabay Content License. A good oil pastel sun. Set aside for the sun by the same child as the flowers.",
    "Flickr, Missouri State Parks, \"Pre-K and Kindergarten, Honorable Mention, Gracie Portell\" (https://www.flickr.com/photos/47969339@N02/52276408118), Public Domain Mark. Small crayon flowers in four colors. Set aside: too small to cut out cleanly and a finer colored-pencil line.",
    "Pixabay, Liziart, \"Crayon Kid Drawing Illustration\" (https://pixabay.com/photos/crayon-kid-drawing-illustration-663940/), Pixabay Content License. Red crayon flower heads with no stems. A good backup source for more flower heads.",
    "Pixabay, pastelila and loveline: crayon flowers, clouds, sprouts, and grass tufts. Rejected: digital crayon brushes, not crayon on paper, and they would mix two kinds of hand in one set.",
    "Pixabay, the crayon cloud and crayon sun-face searches: no real crayon cloud on white turned up with a confirmed license; the sun face sits on a blue scribbled sky that cannot be separated."
